    "registration": {
      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "LIANG Kuo-chih 梁國治 (T. 階平, H. 瑤峯, 豐山), Nov. 18, 1723–1787, Jan. 31, official and calligrapher, was a native of K'uai-chi, Chekiang. After taking his chü-jên degree in 1741 he passed a special examination which gave him the post of secretary of the Grand Secretariat.",
